### Proposal to improve performance

### Description
While investigating potential instruction-level optimizations for the AWQ CUDA GEMM kernel (`gemm_forward_4bit_cuda_m16nXk32` in csrc/libtorch_stable/quantization/awq/gemm_kernels.cu), I ran an Nsight Compute (`ncu`) profile to evaluate the bottlenecks. 

The profile reveals that the hand-written CUDA kernel is heavily memory-bound, specifically at the L1/TEX cache layer, rather than compute-bound. 

