**Optimization**
Premise -
For $N=128$, the loop executes 8 times. You currently use 8 inline PTX instructions inside the loop (4 sub.f16x2 + 4 fma.rn.f16x2). Precomputing the scaled zero outside the loop adds 8 instructions to the preamble but removes 4 instructions from the inner loop.
Total instructions saved per thread per block: $4 \text{ instructions} \times (N/16) - 8 \text{ setup instructions}$. For $N=128$, this is a net reduction of 24 PTX instructions per thread.

